            <ArticleTitle>An innovative mindfulness and educational care approach in an adult patient affected by gastroesophageal reflux: the IARA model.</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1515/jcim-2016-0154</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">/j/jcim.2017.14.issue-4/jcim-2016-0154/jcim-2016-0154.xml</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Patients affected by gastroesophageal reflux disease (GERD) have a poor quality of life caused by several manifestations such as cough, asthma, laryngitis and dental erosion. The clinical conditions are highly disabling for patients and symptoms are difficult to manage. These conditions lead to many discomforts which contribute to an increase of the disease perception. For these reasons, it is important to improve the interventions on psychological aspects that ameliorate the patients' quality of life. The application of IARA model has proven useful to decrease GERD symptoms, distress and medication intake and to increase adherence to care, improving the patient's quality of life.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
